    "updated_at": "2026-11-19T01:35:10Z",
    "body": "Looks already fixed on upstream/main cd753d468: tilt_a180, first_4axis_part, and an MCP run in mm pass without a change.\n\nPR #2157 (merge commit 81f24951e; commits e955c9dfe and 5b1b1afa5 for issue #2133) landed this fix before v0.24.0.\n\nChecks on clean upstream/main cd753d468:\n- `cargo test -p camcraft-app --test tilt_a180`: 2 passed (`out_of_range_tilt_refuses_by_name_with_a0_b180_remedy`, `a0_b180_slot_cuts_along_machine_x_like_the_other_faces`).\n- `cargo test -p camcraft-app --test first_4axis_part`: 4 passed (including `each_flat_posts_the_same_cut_after_its_index` and `the_first_4axis_part_posts_its_indexed_program`).\n- `cargo test -p camcraft-app --test tilt_basis_compat`: 7 passed (including `live_json_tilts_use_current_basis_and_preserve_an_explicit_legacy_basis`).\n- MCP run in mm (`Tormach 770MX + microARC 4`, `Tormach PathPilot`, 50 mm bar stock, `EM-0600-4FL`, `Slot` from `(10, 0)` to `(30, 0)` at `A0`, `A90`, `A-90`, and `A0/B180` via `add_operation`, `edit_operation`, and `save_project`/`open_project`): every section posted `G1 X10 Y0 Z24.5 F300` and `G1 X30 Y0 Z24.5 F400`, with `G0 A180` on the A0/B180 sections.\n- `tilt {a_deg: 180.0}` refuses with `\"Tool axis A (180 deg) must be in -90..90 deg (Tool axis B -180..180 deg) - for the face opposite the top, use Tool axis A 0 and Tool axis B 180\"`.\n\nLive JSON calls (`project::params_from_json`) and the UI Tilt toggle set `basis_version: 1`. Only a pre-v65 `.camproj` tilt without `basis_version` keeps `basis_version: 0` on load and partial edits.\n\nSuggest closing; the maintainer decides.\n",
    "author_association": "COLLABORATOR",
