    "updated_at": "2026-11-19T07:43:00Z",
    "body": "fix on issue/2599-a180-legacy-basis · PR #2730 · pinned by tilt_a180_routes::a_legacy_tilt_edited_to_a0_b180_on_the_operation_page_posts_the_same_local_xy, tilt_a180_routes::a_legacy_tilt_edited_to_a0_b180_over_mcp_posts_the_same_local_xy, tilt_a180_routes::a0_a90_a_minus_90_and_a0_b180_post_the_same_local_xy · merges when reviewed\n\nThe defect is still on main for a tilt from an old file (no `basis_version`, basis 0). When the user sets the angles to A0/B180 on the operation page or with MCP `edit_operation`, the tilt keeps basis 0. The slot from (10,0) to (30,0) then posts `G1 X0 Y-10` -> `X0 Y-30`. New operations post correct XY at A0, A90, A-90 and A0/B180. The fix gives basis 1 to a tilt when an edit changes its angles.\n",
